{"files":[{"content":"#include <cstdint>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <limits>\n#include <vector>\n\nclass FastInput {\n    enum { buffer_size = 1 << 20 };\n    char buffer_[buffer_size];\n    std::size_t position_ = 0;\n    std::size_t size_ = 0;\n\n    bool next(char& character) {\n        if (position_ == size_) {\n            size_ = std::fread(buffer_, 1, buffer_size, stdin);\n            position_ = 0;\n            if (size_ == 0) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n        character = buffer_[position_++];\n        return true;\n    }\n\npublic:\n    bool read_int(int& result) {\n        char character = 0;\n        do {\n            if (!next(character)) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        } while (static_cast<unsigned char>(character) <= ' ');\n\n        bool negative = false;\n        if (character == '-' || character == '+') {\n            negative = character == '-';\n            if (!next(character)) {\n                return false;\n            }\n        }\n\n        std::int64_t value = 0;\n        do {\n            value = value * 10 + (character - '0');\n            if (!next(character)) {\n                break;\n            }\n        } while (character >= '0' && character <= '9');\n\n        result = static_cast<int>(negative ? -value : value);\n        return true;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastInput input;\n    int n = 0;\n    int s = 0;\n    if (!input.read_int(n) || !input.read_int(s)) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> ring(static_cast<std::size_t>(s) * width);\n    std::vector<std::int64_t> column_sums(width, 0);\n    int* const ring_begin = ring.data();\n    int* const ring_end = ring_begin + ring.size();\n    int* slot = ring_begin;\n    std::int64_t maximum = std::numeric_limits<std::int64_t>::min();\n\n    for (int row = 0; row < s; ++row) {\n        for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n            int value = 0;\n            input.read_int(value);\n            slot[column] = value;\n            column_sums[column] += value;\n        }\n        slot += n;\n    }\n    if (slot == ring_end) {\n        slot = ring_begin;\n    }\n\n    std::int64_t window_sum = 0;\n    for (int column = 0; column < s; ++column) {\n        window_sum += column_sums[column];\n    }\n    maximum = window_sum;\n    for (int column = s; column < n; ++column) {\n        window_sum += column_sums[column] - column_sums[column - s];\n        if (window_sum > maximum) {\n            maximum = window_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int row = s; row < n; ++row) {\n        for (int column = 0; column < n; ++column) {\n            int value = 0;\n            input.read_int(value);\n            column_sums[column] += static_cast<std::int64_t>(value) - slot[column];\n            slot[column] = value;\n        }\n        slot += n;\n        if (slot == ring_end) {\n            slot = ring_begin;\n        }\n\n        window_sum = 0;\n        for (int column = 0; column < s; ++column) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[column];\n        }\n        if (window_sum > maximum) {\n            maximum = window_sum;\n        }\n        for (int column = s; column < n; ++column) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[column] - column_sums[column - s];\n            if (window_sum > maximum) {\n                maximum = window_sum;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", static_cast<long long>(maximum));\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"The fastest archived compact streaming implementation should remain the best full-program candidate: it reduces computation to O(N²), minimizes stored data to S contiguous rows, and avoids observed ARM64 SIMD/OpenMP overheads.","notes":"Conservatively retain the measured-fastest archived design unchanged; no unmeasured combination with slower SIMD or OpenMP variants is introduced.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":["73efb39efa4b478e"],"transformations":["Replace fragmented full-matrix storage and S-dependent traversal with contiguous S-row ring storage plus contiguous per-column vertical sums.","Separate initial ring filling from overwrite rows, then evaluate each vertical window with a contiguous horizontal rolling sum and 64-bit maximum.","Use buffered signed-integer input while preserving the required standard input/output contract."]}